From e7f3eb426657a0885cf9dda947042a598eb43099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mat Kowalski <mko@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 13:49:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/26] MCO: harden bgp-vip-config ingestion

Degrade instead of blanking peers when the ConfigMap disappears on a
live BGP cluster, validate and compact the JSON payload at both
ingestion points, strip the trailing newline from the rendered peer
file, and tighten the new RBAC to the single ConfigMap actually read.
---
